Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): FORK_PR_URL

Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patch `26-fairy-rings` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`c2492318d`).

**Problem.** Fairy rings did nothing.

**Change.** New modules `content/travel/fairy-rings` + pack, on the cache's `fairyring` dbtable:
- Configure (Dramen or Lunar staff) opens the dial (398) with the travel log (381); dial buttons and 'Use code' set `fairyring_1..3`.
- Confirm, Zanaris and Last-destination teleport (`fairyring_lastloc_opvis` drives the op text); the log lists visited codes.
- A code with no ring, or the ring you stand in, does not move you.
- On teleport the travel log's search input (meslayer mode 28, which the client opens) is closed with `meslayer_close`: `meslayer_ondialogabort` does not cover mode 28.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: varps `fairyring_travel*` 63784-63785 (visited codes).

**Tests.** `FairyRingScriptTest` (integration).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** Codes and destinations from the cache's `fairyring` dbtable. The no-move rule follows the OSRS Wiki's Fairy ring page (a fact, nothing copied).

**Caveats.**
- No favourites, hideout sequence or per-ring quest requirements.

**Release note.** Fairy rings work: dial, travel log, Zanaris and Last-destination.

